---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Building Code Consulting & Construction Compliance Services" description="Burnham's code consultants, led by an ICC-certified architect, provide due diligence, life safety, ADA accessibility and special services for projects nationwide." nav="what-we-do">
  <div class="page-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ol class="crumbs"><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li>What we do</li><li>Code consulting</li></ol>
      <nav aria-label="On this page"><a href="#due-diligence">Due diligence</a><a href="#life-safety">Life safety</a><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a><a href="#special">Special services</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></nav>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="stack">
        <h1 class="h-display">Code consulting, <span class="hl-block">simplified.</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">Burnham’s code consultants sit on national and municipal code drafting committees, stay in constant contact with building officials, and teach code compliance at seminars and universities. They review new and existing buildings so the department of buildings can approve plans promptly.</p>
        <div class="row">
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Get started with your plans</a>
          <a class="btn btn--outline" href="/code-consulting-process/">Our code consulting process</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="media media--tall"><img src="/assets/img/services/code-team-review.jpg" alt="Two Burnham code consultants reviewing a project on a laptop" width="1800" height="1013"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark section--tight">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="stack stack--sm">
        <div class="eyebrow">Beyond life safety</div>
        <p class="h-section" style="font-size: clamp(24px, 2.6vw, 34px); line-height: 1.25;">Other consultants stop at egress, sprinklers and fire alarms. We also review zoning, historic preservation, site planning and energy conservation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stack stack--sm">
        <p class="body">Complex facilities raise complex code issues, so seasoned professionals belong in a project’s earliest phases. Our consultants are experts in these codes and standards:</p>
        <ul class="tags">
          <li class="tag">Building</li><li class="tag">Accessibility</li><li class="tag">Electrical</li><li class="tag">Mechanical</li><li class="tag">Plumbing</li><li class="tag">Energy</li><li class="tag">Sprinkler</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="media media--tall"><img src="/assets/img/services/code-experience.jpg" alt="Burnham team members reviewing documents in the office" width="1800" height="1013" loading="lazy"></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <div class="eyebrow">Experience in construction codes</div>
        <h2 class="h-section">Led by an ICC-certified architect with more than four decades of experience.</h2>
        <p class="body">The code team is led by a licensed, International Code Council-certified architect and includes several licensed professionals. They apply that knowledge to a broad range of project types:</p>
        <ul class="list list--cols">
          <li>Large-scale mixed-use developments</li>
          <li>Historic building renovations</li>
          <li>Universities and schools</li>
          <li>Residential towers</li>
          <li>Hotels</li>
          <li>Business and mercantile build-outs</li>
          <li>Medical facilities</li>
          <li>Movie theatres</li>
          <li>Transportation facilities</li>
          <li>Data centers and mission-critical facilities</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" id="due-diligence">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="stack">
        <span class="chip">Service 01</span>
        <h2 class="h-section">Due diligence</h2>
        <p class="body">Buying or selling a building, satisfying lender refinancing requirements, or raising a building’s valuation while reducing risk. Our due diligence review covers:</p>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>Municipal records and technical evaluation</li>
          <li>Fire, life safety and accessibility on-site survey</li>
          <li>Document and floor plan review</li>
          <li>Code and zoning assessment</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout">
          <div class="callout__title">The deliverable</div>
          <div class="callout__body">A comprehensive report that identifies compliance issues so they can be corrected before the space goes to market.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="media media--tall"><img src="/assets/img/services/due-diligence.jpg" alt="Consultants marking up architectural drawings at a table" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="life-safety">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="media media--tall"><img src="/assets/img/services/life-safety.jpg" alt="A consultant in a hard hat and safety vest measuring a window opening on site" width="1500" height="1855" loading="lazy"></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <span class="chip">Service 02</span>
        <h2 class="h-section">Life safety</h2>
        <p class="body">We review life safety and advise on code from schematic design through final construction documents, and can review sites once construction is underway. We help develop a compliance plan with readily achievable solutions for:</p>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>Fire alarm systems</li>
          <li>Egress</li>
          <li>Sprinklers</li>
          <li>Accessibility on-site surveys</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="body">The code team recommends modifications before plan submittal, limiting building department corrections and saving time in review.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" id="accessibility">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="stack">
        <span class="chip">Service 03</span>
        <h2 class="h-section">ADA &amp; accessibility</h2>
        <p class="body">The code group can review drawings as early as schematic design, advising on current Americans with Disabilities Act requirements and flagging any changes needed. Our accessibility work spans building alteration projects at every level of regulation:</p>
        <ul class="tags">
          <li class="tag">Local</li><li class="tag">State</li><li class="tag">Federal</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="body">Early assistance and expert code analysis save time and money during permit review, construction and site inspections.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="media media--tall"><img src="/assets/img/services/accessibility.jpg" alt="A hand holding a stainless steel grab bar mounted on a bathroom wall" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="special">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="media media--tall"><img src="/assets/img/services/special-services.jpg" alt="A Burnham-branded hard hat and safety vest resting on rolled drawings" width="1800" height="1200" loading="lazy"></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <span class="chip">Service 04</span>
        <h2 class="h-section">Special services</h2>
        <p class="body">The code group supports the entire project cycle, from design through plan review to final construction, and steps in on critical issues as they arise.</p>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>Closing outstanding building violations</li>
          <li>Expert witness services</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout">
          <div class="callout__title">Paired with permitting</div>
          <div class="callout__body">Code consulting works alongside our <a class="link" href="/what-we-do/permit-management/">permit management</a> team, including the phased permitting Burnham pioneered so construction can continue while plans are finalized.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" id="faq">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2">
      <div class="stack stack--sm">
        <div class="eyebrow">FAQ</div>
        <h2 class="h-section">Building code consulting questions.</h2>
        <p class="body">Have a question that isn’t answered here? <a class="link" href="/contact/">Ask our code team</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>What is the benefit of using Burnham’s code consulting services?</summary>
          <div class="faq__a"><p>Our consultants understand all relevant municipal codes and sit on national and municipal code drafting committees. Comprehensive reviews of zoning, historic preservation, site planning and energy conservation help building officials approve your plans promptly, saving time and money.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>When should I bring in a code consultant?</summary>
          <div class="faq__a"><p>In the early phases of a project, to keep it on schedule. It is especially valuable for large mixed-use developments, historic renovations and projects with complex code requirements, and when satisfying lender refinancing requirements, raising a building’s valuation or reducing risk in a sale or purchase.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How does code consulting help my timeline?</summary>
          <div class="faq__a"><p>We identify compliance issues early. Reviewing life safety from schematic design through construction documents lets us recommend changes before submittal, which limits building department corrections and prevents delays during construction and inspections.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How much do your code consulting services cost?</summary>
          <div class="faq__a"><p>Like our other services, code consulting is typically offered at a flat rate. That allows precise budgeting and avoids the unpredictable costs of hourly billing.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>My project is already underway. Can you still help?</summary>
          <div class="faq__a"><p>Yes. We can review sites after construction has begun, advise on solutions to critical safety issues, help close outstanding building violations and serve as an expert witness.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What types of projects do you handle?</summary>
          <div class="faq__a"><p>Large mixed-use developments, historic renovations, universities and schools, residential towers, hotels, business and mercantile build-outs, medical facilities, movie theatres, transportation facilities and data centers.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What is included?</summary>
          <div class="faq__a"><p>Services are tailored to each project and fall into four categories: due diligence, life safety, accessibility and special services. Our consultants cover building, accessibility, electrical, mechanical, plumbing, energy and sprinkler codes and standards.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where do you offer code consulting?</summary>
          <div class="faq__a"><p>Nationwide. Our team stays current on code interpretations by working with municipal building officials across the country, covering local, state and federal requirements.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What other services do you offer?</summary>
          <div class="faq__a"><p><a class="link" href="/what-we-do/permit-management/">Permit management</a> for new construction through nationwide expansion, plus licensing, public way services and land use and zoning.</p></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap cta-block">
      <div class="stack stack--sm">
        <h2>Have a code question on a current project?</h2>
        <p>Send us the drawings or the issue. A member of the code team will advise on the provisions that apply.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Talk to our code team</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
